{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/894200-humanity-breaking-points-and-touchstones-question","id":894200,"title":"Humanity, Breaking Points and Touchstones Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-19T11:40:04-07:00","id":894200,"title":"Humanity, Breaking Points and Touchstones Question","content":"So I have decided to give 2nd ed a second read through/chance and I am liking it much more this time.<br /> <br /> One thing I am getting confused on is the differentiation between &quot;Attached Touchstones&quot;, &quot;No Touchstones&quot; and what I assume is &quot;Unattached Touchstones&quot; (although that term is never used, just implied).<br /> <br /> I can interpret it one of two ways:<br /> You have one or more attached touchstones (meaning you have a dot in Humanity track next to it) +2 or +3 to your roll.<br /> You have a Touchstone that is unattached (meaning the touchstone is alive, but your humanity has dropped so no dots next to them) +0 to your roll.<br /> All your Touchstones are gone, as in destroyed/dead. -2 to your roll.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> You have one or more attached touchstones (meaning you have a dot in Humanity track next to it) +2 or +3 to your roll.<br /> You either have all your Touchstones dead and/or they are all unattached -2 to your roll.<br /> <br /> While we are at it, when you lose your last touchstone, you immediately lose a point of Humanity. Does this mean detached as well as dead/destroyed?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11830-joboo","name":"Joboo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:58:03-07:00","id":894215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/894200-humanity-breaking-points-and-touchstones-question#post894200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have decided to give 2nd ed a second read through/chance and I am liking it much more this time.<br /> <br /> One thing I am getting confused on is the differentiation between &amp;quot;Attached Touchstones&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;No Touchstones&amp;quot; and what I assume is &amp;quot;Unattached Touchstones&amp;quot; (although that term is never used, just implied).<br /> <br /> I can interpret it one of two ways:<br /> You have one or more attached touchstones (meaning you have a dot in Humanity track next to it) +2 or +3 to your roll.<br /> You have a Touchstone that is unattached (meaning the touchstone is alive, but your humanity has dropped so no dots next to them) +0 to your roll.<br /> All your Touchstones are gone, as in destroyed/dead. -2 to your roll.<br /> <br /> OR<br /> <br /> You have one or more attached touchstones (meaning you have a dot in Humanity track next to it) +2 or +3 to your roll.<br /> You either have all your Touchstones dead and/or they are all unattached -2 to your roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>The former is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/894200-humanity-breaking-points-and-touchstones-question#post894200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While we are at it, when you lose your last touchstone, you immediately lose a point of Humanity. Does this mean detached as well as dead/destroyed?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, only if they die or are otherwise destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T11:58:18-07:00","id":894216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Joboo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/894200-humanity-breaking-points-and-touchstones-question#post894200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You have one or more attached touchstones (meaning you have a dot in Humanity track next to it) +2 or +3 to your roll.<br /> You have a Touchstone that is unattached (meaning the touchstone is alive, but your humanity has dropped so no dots next to them) +0 to your roll.<br /> All your Touchstones are gone, as in destroyed/dead. -2 to your roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While we are at it, when you lose your last touchstone, you immediately lose a point of Humanity. Does this mean detached as well as dead/destroyed? </div> </div> </div>Only destroyed.<br /> <br /> The terminology was confusing at first glance for me too. My quick explanation is cellphones. Your cellphone running out of minutes (detached) sucks, but at least you can recharge it eventually and maybe use it for apps in the meantime. Losing (Destroying) your cellphone is a whole different nightmare.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-19T12:31:23-07:00","id":894236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/894200-humanity-breaking-points-and-touchstones-question?p=894216#post894216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My quick explanation is cellphones. Your cellphone running out of minutes (detached) sucks, but at 